findings.scenario:
1. A private session's chain stops after its deposit (a lock, or giveme.my), leaving box B unmixed.
2. The user presses Bring it back anyway. The warning says only "anyone can tie your deposit to your private balance".
3. In withdrawOne, received is false because a recorded chain made B. depositAccountOf returns undefined for a session's chain. So origin stays undefined and the history entry reads boxFrom(tx).
4. The next stealth mint or private pool start ranks it 0 and takes it whenever it pays alone.

The new Seedelf is then tied, for anyone, to the deposit, the one-time account and the funding's private inputs. Where that funding was money made private, the tie reaches the public account. This is exactly the link the stealth mint is meant to avoid. The note still says boxes keep the Seedelf apart.

The same class comes from:
- a private Bootstrap's box brought back by hand;
- Bring every box back now;
- the retired pools' run, with no press at all;
- a session collateral box left by "Bring the rest back now";
- an unsure box brought back anyway (unknown origin, possibly a stranger's).

Before (b) it ranked after received money. tests/lovejoin-someone-else.test.ts:256-257 pins this: the own deposit's way back has no origin.

